  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nWe propose an iterative projected gradient descent algorithm with feasibility maintenance and Lagrangian-based constraint handling. The method minimizes the maximum overlap integral while respecting the constraints [0,1] and the integral normalization. The key idea is to alternately tighten the worst-case overlap while maintaining feasibility through implicit constraints.\n\nBottleneck: Bilinear constraints in h lead to non-convex optimization. We handle this by local linearization and gradient-based updates, projecting back to feasible region after each step.\n\nLimitation: Convergence is to local minima; however, the projection step ensures feasibility at every iteration.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nProblem variables:\n- h \u2208 [0,1]^(n_points)\n- C scalar, representing maximum overlap\n\nObjective:\nMinimize C such that:\n\n1. C \u2265 (np.correlate(h, 1 - h, mode='full')) * dx for all possible lags\n2. sum(h) = n_points / 2\n3. 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n\nFeasibility projection:\n- After any update, clip h to [0,1]\n- Rescale h to maintain sum(h) = n_points / 2\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na. Initialization\n   1. If initial_h_values available, start with normalized and clipped version\n   2. Else, initialize h to 0.5 * np.ones(n_points), clip, and normalize\n   3. Set best_h = h.copy(), best_C = evaluate_C(h)\n\nb. Main loop for iterations until time budget exhausted:\n   i. Current_C = evaluate_C(h)\n   ii. If Current_C < best_C:\n       - Update best_h and best_C\n   iii. Compute cross-correlation c = np.correlate(h, 1 - h, mode='full')\n   iv. Identify all lags k where c[k] is near maximum (e.g., top 5% contributions)\n   v. For each of these k:\n       A. Compute gradient of h with respect to the overlap at k:\n           \u2207h = (1 - h[k + x]) for valid x indices overlapping with h shifted by k\n       B. Update h using a scaled gradient step: h = h - \u03b1 * \u2207h\n       C. Project h to [0,1] and rescale to maintain sum\n   vi. Decrease step size \u03b1 on lack of improvement (e.g., \u03b1 *= 0.95)\n   vii. Track progress and update best solution\n\nc. Feasibility projection:\n   1. Clip h to [0,1]\n   2. Compute scaling factor s = (n_points/2) / sum(h)\n   3. h = s * h\n\nd. Termination:\n   - Return best_h, best_C, n_points after budget exhaustion or convergence\n\n4. Search choices and variations\n   - Initial step size \u03b1 = 0.1\n   - Step decrease factor = 0.95 on backtracking\n   - Max of 1000 iterations within 1100s\n   - Focus on top 5% contributing lags to maximize impact\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n   - Each iteration: ~1ms, target 1000 iterations\n   - Projection ensures feasibility\n   - Step decrease avoids stagnation\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n   - Check best_h is feasible and C computed correctly",
